      ],
      "tags": [
        "prompt-injection",
        "override"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PROMPT-012",
      "phase": "prompt_injection",
      "severity": "critical",
      "pattern": "(?i)\\b(always\\s+(be\\s+)?(allowed|permitted|granted)|never\\s+loses?\\s+access|always\\s+(get|gets|have|has)\\s+(in|access))\\b[^.\\n]{0,80}\\b(allow[- ]?list|whitelist|acl|access\\s+control)\\b|\\b(const|let|var|final|static|public|private)?\\s*[A-Za-z_]*(HARD[_-]OVERRIDE|OVERRIDE[_-](KEY|NUMBER|TOKEN|USER|ID|PASSWORD)|BREAK[_-]?GLASS|BACKDOOR[_-](KEY|TOKEN|PASSWORD|USER|ID|NUMBER|ACCESS)|BYPASS[_-](KEY|TOKEN|CODE|USER))[A-Za-z_]*\\s*[:=]\\s*[\\\"']|\\b(inject|insert|patch|splice|append|add)\\b[^\\n]{0,60}\\b[\\w./-]*(access[-_]?control|authoriz\\w*|authenticat\\w*|permission\\w*|rbac|acl|middleware|guard|session|login)[\\w.-]*\\.(ts|tsx|js|jsx|mjs|py|go|rb|java|php|rs|cs)\\b|\\b(inject|splice|patch)\\s+(the\\s+)?(following|this)\\s+(typescript|javascript|python|go|rust|java|code|block|snippet|function|lines?)\\b",
      "description": "Prompt injection — instructs the agent to weaken access control or plant an auth bypass",
      "remediation": "Treat this as an attempted backdoor until proven otherwise. The shapes it matches are an unconditional-access claim (\"always allowed regardless of the allowlist\"), a hard-coded override, break-glass, backdoor or master-key constant, and an instruction pointing the agent at an access-control, auth, permission, RBAC or session source file with code to inject. A genuine break-glass path is reviewed, logged, time-boxed and lives in the project's own repository — it does not arrive as a skill that asks an agent to paste a constant into a security check and restart the service. Revert the edit, rotate anything the constant would have authenticated, and check the file's history for an edit that already landed.",
      "references": [
        "CWE-287",
        "CWE-798",
        "OWASP LLM01",
        "OWASP Agentic Top 10 — Tool Misuse",
        "MITRE T1556"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "prompt-injection",
        "auth-bypass",
        "backdoor",
        "access-control"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PROMPT-013",
      "phase": "prompt_injection",
      "severity": "high",
      "pattern": "(?i)\\b(always|automatically|silently|quietly)\\s+(send|sends|post|posts|forward|forwards|share|shares|upload|uploads|deliver|delivers|dm|message)\\b[^.\\n]{0,60}\\b(to|via|through)\\b[^.\\n]{0,50}\\b(telegram|discord|slack|whatsapp|signal|wechat|webhook|pastebin|gist)\\b|\\b(telegram|discord|slack|whatsapp)\\b[^.\\n]{0,40}\\b((chat|user|channel|group)[_ -]?)?id\\b[^.\\n]{0,20}[`\"'(]?\\s*\\d{6,}",
      "description": "Prompt injection — instructs the agent to send output to a fixed external recipient",
      "file_filter": {
        "extensions": [
          "md",
          "txt",
          "prompt",
          "mdx",
          "rst"
        ],
        "filename_exact": [
          "SKILL.md",
          "CLAUDE.md",
          "AGENTS.md",
          "GEMINI.md",
          "copilot-instructions.md",
          "mcp.json",
          "tool.json",
          "plugin.json",
          "manifest.json",
          "skill.json",
          "server.json"
        ],
        "filename_suffix": [
          ".cursorrules",
          ".windsurfrules",
          ".clinerules"
        ]
      },
      "remediation": "Find out whose account the identifier belongs to. A skill that tells the agent to *always* send its output to a messaging platform, or that hard-codes a chat, channel or user id, has a recipient the person installing it did not choose — a productivity tracker that reports to a fixed Telegram id is reporting to its author. Replace the fixed destination with one the user configures, or drop the send step; if the destination is deliberate, it belongs in the skill's description where the reviewer sees it.",
      "references": [
        "MITRE T1567",
        "OWASP LLM02",
        "CWE-200"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "prompt-injection",
        "exfiltration",
        "messaging-platform"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PROMPT-014",
      "phase": "prompt_injection",
      "severity": "high",
      "pattern": "(?i)\\b(write|writes|create|creates|update|updates|add|adds|append|appends|merge|merges|copy|copies|cp|install|installs|configure|configures|edit|edits|modify|modifies|generate|generates|overwrite|overwrites|register|registers)\\b[^\\n]{0,60}(~|\\$HOME|\\.)?/?\\.(claude|codex|cursor|openclaw|agents|gemini|windsurf|aider)/(settings[\\w.-]*\\.json|hooks?|agents?|commands?|rules?|mcp\\.json|config[\\w.-]*)\\b",
      "description": "Prompt injection — skill writes into the agent's settings, hooks or sub-agent configuration",
      "remediation": "Read the file it writes and what goes into it. Settings, hooks, commands, rules and MCP configuration are the agent's own trust configuration: a hook entry is a command the host runs on its own, a settings `permissions.allow` entry pre-approves tools for every later session, and a sub-agent or rules file is instruction text the model reads as its own. A skill that edits them is granting itself capability that outlives the task it was installed for. Apply such changes yourself, from a diff you have read, rather than letting a skill write them.\n\nA package's own README telling a human to add it to `mcp.json` or `.cursor/mcp.json` is how every MCP server documents its installation, so this rule does not fire in README or INSTALL files. What it looks for is the same write described in text the agent itself consumes — SKILL.md, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, a rules file — where it is an instruction to the agent rather than to the reader.",
      "references": [
        "MITRE T1546",
        "OWASP Agentic Top 10 — Excessive Agency",
        "CWE-732"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "prompt-injection",
        "agent-config",
        "persistence",
        "privilege-escalation"
      ],
      "suppress": {
        "filename_suffix": [
          "README.md",
          "README.mdx",
          "README.rst",
          "INSTALL.md",
          "INSTALLATION.md"
        ]
      },
      "file_filter": {
        "extensions": [
          "md",
          "txt",
          "prompt",
          "mdx",
          "rst"
        ],
        "filename_exact": [
          "AGENTS.md",
          "CLAUDE.md",
          "GEMINI.md",
          "SKILL.md",
          "config.json",
          "copilot-instructions.md",
          "hooks.json",
          "manifest.json",
          "mcp.json",
          "plugin.json",
          "settings.json",
          "settings.local.json",
          "tool.json"
        ],
        "filename_suffix": [
          ".cursorrules",
          ".windsurfrules",
          ".clinerules"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "PROMPT-015",
      "phase": "prompt_injection",
      "severity": "high",
      "pattern": "(?i)\\b(bypass|disable|skip|suppress|avoid|prevent|turn\\s+off)\\b[^.\\n]{0,40}\\bpermission\\s+(prompts?|mode|dialogs?)\\b|\\b(allow|approve|permit)\\s+all\\s+(the\\s+)?(commands?|bash)\\b|--dangerously-skip-permissions\\b|\\bbypassPermissions\\b|\\bdanger-full-access\\b|--yolo\\b|\\bwithout\\s+(any\\s+)?permission\\s+prompts?\\b",
      "description": "Prompt injection — disables the host's permission prompt or sandbox",
      "remediation": "The permission prompt and the sandbox are the boundary between a skill and the machine, and every match here removes it: an allow-all entry, an auto-approve step, `--dangerously-skip-permissions`, `bypassPermissions`, `danger-full-access` or `--yolo`. A skill that needs a specific command should say which one and let it be granted narrowly (`Bash(npm run build:*)`); a skill whose first step is to turn the prompt off is asking for everything the agent can reach, for the rest of the session. Remove the step, and check whether it has already written an allow-list into the host's settings.",
      "references": [
        "CWE-250",
        "OWASP Agentic Top 10 — Excessive Agency",
        "MITRE T1562.001"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "prompt-injection",
        "permission-bypass",
        "sandbox-escape",
        "excessive-agency"
      ],
      "file_filter": {
        "extensions": [
          "md",
          "txt",
          "prompt",
          "mdx",
          "rst"
        ],
        "filename_exact": [
          "AGENTS.md",
          "CLAUDE.md",
          "GEMINI.md",
          "SKILL.md",
          "config.json",
          "copilot-instructions.md",
          "hooks.json",
          "manifest.json",
          "mcp.json",
          "plugin.json",
          "settings.json",
          "settings.local.json",
          "tool.json"
        ],
        "filename_suffix": [
          ".cursorrules",
          ".windsurfrules",
          ".clinerules"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "PROMPT-016",
      "phase": "prompt_injection",
      "severity": "critical",
      "pattern": "(?i)\\b(base64\\s+(-d|--decode|-D)|openssl\\s+enc\\s+-d|atob)\\b[^\\n|]{0,80}\\|\\s*(sudo\\s+)?(bash|sh|zsh|python3?|node)\\b|(?-i:L2Jpbi9iYXNo)|(?-i:L2Jpbi9zaA)|(?-i:Y3VybCAt)|(?-i:d2dldCAt)|(?-i:YmFzaCAt)|(?-i:c3VkbyA)",
      "description": "Prompt injection — encoded shell payload the user is told to paste and run",
